      "seed": 101,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 556925296,
      "customData": {
        "title": "Introducing Private Pass",
        "spoken": "Hi, my project is called Private Pass. I wanted to find out whether an event could check that a ticket belongs to the right person, without storing everybody's face in one central database. I also wanted the entrance check to work without internet. I built a working prototype, and I'll show you how it works, how I made my decisions, and what my testing did and didn't prove.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Ticket must belong to the right person.\n2. No central face database; gate works offline.\n3. Show the build, the tests and the limits.",
        "originalSlideText": "Private Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n01\nEVENT ENTRY  /  SOFTWARE PROJECT\nPrivate Pass\nOne ticket. \nOne person.\nEntry checks that work offline,\nwithout a central face database.\nOFFLINE ENTRY\nFACE CHECK\nDATA MINIMISATION\nTHE ENTRY JOURNEY\nREGISTER\nGET PASS\nVERIFY\nGate makes the entry decision \nlocally\n.",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 1"
        ],
        "claim": "Introducing Private Pass"
      },
