    {
      "id": "story-frame-17",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "name": "Slide 17",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#202020",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 117,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 851904912,
      "customData": {
        "title": "What I learned",
        "spoken": "The biggest lesson for me was that building something and proving it works are two different jobs. I got carried away adding features because I wanted the whole process to feel real. But that gave me less time for testing. If I did this again, I would stop adding features sooner and save a clear test record each time I finished something. I'd also test face matching on new examples, instead of just checking it on the examples I used while building it.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Building is different from proving.\n2. Stop adding features earlier.\n3. Save records and test on new examples.",
        "originalSlideText": "LESSONS\nWhat I would do differently next time.\nI spent too long adding features and not enough time testing.\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n16\n01\nSTOP ADDING FEATURES SOONER\nAdding tickets made the product complete, but reduced testing time.\n02\nSAVE TEST EVIDENCE WHILE BUILDING\nRecord device details, steps, logs and outcomes.\n03\nTEST ON FRESH EXAMPLES\nSet thresholds first; use new cases for evaluation.",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 17"
        ],
        "claim": "What I learned"
      },
      "index": "b2h",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793173192618,
      "link": null
    },
